# Staging-only automation

Follow the repository-root `AGENTS.md` for every task.

- Use a dedicated `cursor/*` or `automation/*` branch.
- Never push directly to `main` and never auto-merge.
- Never connect to or deploy production.
- Do not change IAM, organization policy, Firestore data, Storage data, or secrets.
- Do not run a broad Functions deploy. Use explicit function names only.
- Treat `scripts/automation/validate-staging-scope.mjs` as a mandatory fail-closed gate.
- If a command needs approval outside the documented allowlist, stop and report the exact blocker.
- Run the smallest relevant tests first; rely on GitHub Actions for the canonical full verification.
- Return the completion fields required by `AGENTS.md`.

